    "description": "Potters Industries manufactures glass beads, microspheres, and related engineered materials used in road markings, runway markings, and specialized industrial applications. Its end markets include transportation safety, infrastructure maintenance, and industrial customers that use reflective media and specialty materials in their operations. The operating model is asset-heavy and manufacturing based, supported by a network of production and logistics sites across North America and Europe. Macquarie stated in November 2025 that Potters operates 26 manufacturing and logistics sites across North America and Europe and has additional presence in South America and Asia, while company materials identify Malvern, Pennsylvania as its global headquarters. Macquarie Asset Management and co-investors including UniSuper and Partners Capital announced an agreement in November 2025 to acquire a majority stake from TJC, but the reviewed sources did not confirm a completed closing or disclose the current post-transaction ownership structure as of the review date.",
